@startuml 3.3.3 - View Client Profile
title Sequence Diagram — 3.3.3 - View Client Profile

autonumber
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam BoxPadding 10
skinparam ParticipantPadding 10

' === Participants ===
actor "User / Agency member" as user_agency_member
boundary "ClientProfileListPage / WorkspaceClientsPage (UI)" as clientprofilelistpage_workspaceclientspage_ui
boundary "ClientProfileController / WorkspaceController" as clientprofilecontroller_workspacecontroller
control "ClientProfileServiceImpl / WorkspaceServiceImpl" as clientprofileserviceimpl_workspaceserviceimpl
entity "ClientProfileRepository / WorkspaceMemberRepository" as clientprofilerepository_workspacememberrepository
entity "client_profiles / workspace_members" as client_profiles_workspace_members

' === Flow ===
user_agency_member -> clientprofilelistpage_workspaceclientspage_ui: opens /client-profiles
clientprofilelistpage_workspaceclientspage_ui -> clientprofilecontroller_workspacecontroller: GET /api/v1/client-profile/mine
clientprofilecontroller_workspacecontroller -> clientprofileserviceimpl_workspaceserviceimpl: listMine(currentUser)
clientprofileserviceimpl_workspaceserviceimpl -> clientprofilerepository_workspacememberrepository: findByUserId(currentUser.getId())
clientprofilerepository_workspacememberrepository -> client_profiles_workspace_members: query by user_id
client_profiles_workspace_members --> clientprofilerepository_workspacememberrepository: List<row> (0..N — a user may own several profiles, e.g. Nike, Adidas)
clientprofileserviceimpl_workspaceserviceimpl -> clientprofilecontroller_workspacecontroller: map rows -> List<ClientProfileResponse>
clientprofilecontroller_workspacecontroller --> clientprofilelistpage_workspaceclientspage_ui: 200 OK List<ClientProfileResponse>
clientprofilelistpage_workspaceclientspage_ui -> user_agency_member: renders one card per brand
user_agency_member -> clientprofilelistpage_workspaceclientspage_ui: opens /workspaces/:id/clients
clientprofilelistpage_workspaceclientspage_ui -> clientprofilecontroller_workspacecontroller: GET /api/v1/workspaces/{id}/members
clientprofilecontroller_workspacecontroller -> clientprofileserviceimpl_workspaceserviceimpl: listMembers(workspaceId)
clientprofileserviceimpl_workspaceserviceimpl -> clientprofilerepository_workspacememberrepository: check workspace exists + caller is active member
clientprofilerepository_workspacememberrepository --> clientprofileserviceimpl_workspaceserviceimpl: active workspace_members rows (joined to client_profiles for CLIENT rows)
clientprofileserviceimpl_workspaceserviceimpl --> clientprofilecontroller_workspacecontroller: List<WorkspaceMemberResponse> (all roles)
clientprofilecontroller_workspacecontroller --> clientprofilelistpage_workspaceclientspage_ui: 200 OK List<WorkspaceMemberResponse>
clientprofilelistpage_workspaceclientspage_ui -> user_agency_member: FE filters role === \"CLIENT\", displays with \"Add client\" action
note over user_agency_member, client_profiles_workspace_members: Note: the backend list endpoint always returns every role (MANAGER/CREATOR/CLIENT) — the Members (/workspaces/:id/members) vs Clients (/workspaces/:id/clients) screen split is a client-side filter, not a separate backend query.

@enduml